{"title":"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1.5_(EXTREMELY_EASY)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1.5 (EXTREMELY EASY)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Extended_Euclid_Algorithm)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Extended Euclid Algorithm)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Mod_11)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Mod 11)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Brute_Force)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Brute Force)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> satisfy the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e9d7ee18fded4c53257b2cc46e83dfd4641dff3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$57x+ 22y = 400$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"17\" />. What is the least possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/d/d3da9f8c7fe0473fdd6f8597eff61d71fedda430.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/a/36a6f557ff4f6d16d75ca66d62f44331f954a4e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 10 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 11 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 13 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 14 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"401\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/2/262d9d8b506e54c524169c8c3e7d0a916f94d363.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"16\" />. Then we have the equation\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/f/2bf0136cc26c0e2fdb02591713b818aad56c3334.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[35x + 22a = 400.\\]\" width=\"132\" height=\"14\" />\nBecause the other two terms are divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/3/7d37d4c647e7e56fd238057a3140c9928c4b872c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> too. Specifically, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/0/e70dc0517fe0e1e20bc4bc99c054945108cced79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=5b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" /> and substitute:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/c/cbcf80e8b90d74e4a4157022659e0d6a7738e508.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[35x + 110b = 400\\]\" width=\"136\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/8/a582b29e015d45d3d72e17773314619e6b0ff523.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[7x + 22b = 80.\\]\" width=\"112\" height=\"14\" />\nAfter some analysis, we find that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/6/626beed3a7eee094ce4b6cf79a49d81669f72d99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=3$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/f/2effc7979b1c93e59356b73253d75e2740b33105.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. In fact, this is the only solution with positive integer solutions. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/2/4d2455ab88c30fff4bd6c79810f0353388a2e12b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = x+y = 5 \\cdot 3 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"221\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~lprado\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1.5_.28EXTREMELY_EASY.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.5_(EXTREMELY_EASY)\">Solution 1.5 (EXTREMELY EASY)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.5 (EXTREMELY EASY)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/c/edcfec15076077c4ab9089a029a9b5d93ed81209.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"17\" /> will always be even. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/3/853c0c1e2d52a87b5a2937d45dbcc081e916217b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$57x$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> must be even for the sum to be an even <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/9/e8924412a12becf7905729885a46e3e351ec5a86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$400$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is even. \n</p><p>Moreover, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/0/6f0b4dca4434f64ccd1a3c5e0a32a1e423997007.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\leq7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/a/d6a4383f4a52eb627a13c937c04e338b8892f94c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor \\frac{400}{57} \\right\\rfloor = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"87\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>So the possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/f/52f430fbb2cfa58db7e9adb00fd02dedca99b477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$400 - 57\\cdot2 = 286 = 22\\cdot13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"217\" height=\"15\" /> works.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfba2d606864d23a563d646cbfce86c7a284c663.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$400 - 57\\cdot4 = 172$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"143\" height=\"15\" /> is not a multiple of 22.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/d/50df33c386c3fe8f02105ab0b5f0db37b7910e10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$400 - 57\\cdot6 = 58$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"134\" height=\"15\" /> is not a multiple of 22.\n</p><p><br />\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/f/2effc7979b1c93e59356b73253d75e2740b33105.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/7/f0760e265c688498d8376016a70a86c33fc69c8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"16\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/f/e6f18709be1f60574df821cd5243f83c3425ab9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"131\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>- unhappyfarmer\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Extended_Euclid_Algorithm.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Extended_Euclid_Algorithm)\">Solution 2 (Extended Euclid Algorithm)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Extended Euclid Algorithm)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We first solve for integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/f/06f8bc07399bcef6cf1cb89d2c3abffdd3b824ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$57x+22y=400$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"17\" />. Use the Extended Euclid Algorithm to find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/7/397fdbb80576dcbd13b2270be2fb8dfd3af02bd6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_1 = -5, y_1 = 13.\\]\" width=\"135\" height=\"16\" /> We multiply both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/e/4ae250d1bdd46e5677f27edcf5efb34587b6fc1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"14\" height=\"11\" /> by 400. Since we require both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> to be positive integers, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/3/4631ea54f049d49f09decdaca2598c97ca89356e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_k = -5 \\cdot 400 + 22k\\]\" width=\"155\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/e/b9e4b7c9fa271159ab8c1a39a0aee6de11e51d04.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y_k = 13 \\cdot 400 - 57k.\\]\" width=\"153\" height=\"16\" /> We can check this method of writing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/d/f5d3dead9cb8d5f6327c737e014850be7a29d0f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/d/c5dd4a48fae40d106f05aa536bdbebd1f0195842.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"11\" /> is valid by substitution into the original equation. Finally, we add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/d/f5d3dead9cb8d5f6327c737e014850be7a29d0f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/d/c5dd4a48fae40d106f05aa536bdbebd1f0195842.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"11\" />, to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/f/c3f0aaae20546fa714dee79553bd5ab269c47e52.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-5 \\cdot 400 + 13 \\cdot 400 - 35k.\\]\" width=\"197\" height=\"14\" /> We want to minimize this value, and after evaluation we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/0/5508487dec3bc5f8d3fc813d5d3b279d797d7919.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3200 - 35k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"89\" height=\"16\" />. Minimizing this value over the positive integers, we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/9/289c17490c8ce6ac211aa25ac2b5d9ddf2b761f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 91$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" />, which yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/3/4a3f5ca66eccd6ca24fc2db4d10eaf2b54bfbf25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Mod_11.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Mod_11)\">Solution 3 (Mod 11)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Mod 11)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Taking mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/d/c1d6f77f7ef87a3089a37646c2e49e47d03d4f7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x\\equiv 4 \\pmod{11}\\iff x\\equiv 2 \\pmod{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"315\" height=\"20\" />. This forces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69271b422e022ea65ff1f288eddfcfa82afd8ab7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> as bigger numbers make the sum pass <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/9/e8924412a12becf7905729885a46e3e351ec5a86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$400$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/a/c4add5fd742ab8f3ea3b8899e8e6ae5674593e98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac{400-2\\cdot 57}{22}=\\frac{200-57}{11}=\\frac{143}{11}=13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"323\" height=\"38\" />. So the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/0/5e0feb68e24a959bbfa19cb47e471cf7d42c9e3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y=2+13=\\boxed{ \\textbf{(E) } 15 }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"205\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~imosilver\n~Minor edits by KINGFIREBOY\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Brute_Force.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Brute_Force)\">Solution 4 (Brute Force)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Brute Force)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>List all the factors of 57 and 22 that are less than 400\n</p><p>Iterate through and find a solution to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69271b422e022ea65ff1f288eddfcfa82afd8ab7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/d/d5d6c134e96b593e23c7196d28274b08f5f31d4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>~Yes i did this during competition \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dLSWVrrKsgs\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dLSWVrrKsgs</a>\n</p><p>~lprado\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B\">2025 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8